				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span id="result_box" lang="en"><span class="hps"><strong> Madonna will open Hard Candy gyms in Peru, Argentina, Brazil and Colombia.</strong> There is already a <strong>Hard Candy gym</strong> in Santiago, Chile. </span></span></p>
<p><span id="result_box" lang="en"><span class="hps">The first <strong>Hard Candy gym</strong> to be opened will be in Buenos Aires, Argentina the first months of 2015. The goal is to open at least 10 new <strong>Hard Candy Fitness gyms</strong> in 5 years in South America: 2 in Rio de Janeiro and Sao Paulo, and 1 in Lima, Buenos Aires, Bogota and Medellin.<br />
</span></span></p>
<p>It was revealed to La Tercera by <span id="result_box" lang="en"><span class="hps">Alex</span> <span class="hps">Wiesner</span>, CEO <span class="hps">and</span> <span class="hps">a member</span> <span class="hps">of</span> <span class="hps">the</span> <span class="hps">Energy Fitness</span> <span class="hps">gym chain</span>, which manages<strong><span class="hps"> Hard</span> <span class="hps">Candy</span> F<span class="hps">itness</span></strong> <span class="hps">in South America</span></span>. There will be an investiment of $ 40 millions.</p>
<p>Other <strong>Madonna&#8217;s Hard Candy gyms</strong> around the world are in Rome (Italy), Berlin (Germany), Sydney (Australia), Toronto (Canada), Mexico City (Mexico), Moskow and St. Petersburg (Russia).</p>
